      },
      "text": "28 December: Pia Glacier and Glacier Alley"
    },
    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:c3205ac1e20a266d",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "db830d8ae037523e04373908b57d5a79f6ea5c9f5e6cbe75dbe6ee008de790bf",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "runId": "ada-en-79efc77a-b889-42c3-95a7-4d1a8db6bd09",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol"
      },
      "text": "The cruise continues overnight through the Gabriel and Magdalena channels and the Cockburn Passage, along the western side of Tierra del Fuego.\n\nThe ship rounds the Brecknock Peninsula and re-enters the Beagle Channel.\n\nYou arrive in Pia Fjord in the morning.\n\nThe group heads towards Pia Glacier in Zodiac boats.\n\nAfter landing, you take a short walk.\n\nThe glacier descends from the mountain peaks to the sea.\n\nIf you prefer, you can take a more challenging route along the old glacier’s lateral moraine.\n\nBack on board, the cruise continues along the Beagle Channel through Glacier Alley.\n\nThe stretch takes its name from the many glaciers descending from the Darwin Range."
    },
